                        "options": [
                          "an engineer",
                          "Mrs Green"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "The structure is…",
                        "options": [
                          "have + object + past participle",
                          "have + past participle + object"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "\"I'll get someone to look at it.\" get + person + …",
                        "options": [
                          "to + verb",
                          "-ing"
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      },
                      {
                        "question": "Why can't the boiler be repaired earlier?",
                        "options": [
                          "The engineer can't come any earlier.",
                          "It's too expensive.",
                          "Mrs Green is away."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "causative",
                    "title": "Causative have and get",
                    "explanation": "«Have» / «get» + objeto + participio indica que otra persona hace algo por nosotros, normalmente un servicio. «Get» es más informal:\n- «I'm having the boiler repaired.» (no lo arreglo yo)\n\nSe usa en cualquier tiempo:\n- «I had my car serviced last week.»\n- «I'm getting the kitchen repainted.»\n- «Could you have the oven checked?»\n\nPara decir a quién le encargas algo: «get» + persona + «to» + verbo, o «have» + persona + verbo:\n- «I'll get someone to look at it.»\n- «I'll have the engineer call you.»\n\nEn español solemos decir «me voy a cortar el pelo», pero en inglés es «I'm going to get my hair cut», porque te lo corta otra persona.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "have + objeto + participio",
                          "I'm having the boiler repaired."
                        ],
                        [
                          "get + objeto + participio",
                          "I'm getting the kitchen repainted."
                        ],
                        [
                          "pasado",
                          "I had my car serviced last week."
                        ],
                        [
                          "con modal",
                          "Could you have the oven checked?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "get + persona + to + verbo",
                          "I'll get someone to look at it."
                        ],
                        [
                          "have + persona + verbo",
                          "I'll have the engineer call you."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm having the boiler repaired on Thursday.",
                      "I'm getting the kitchen repainted next month.",
                      "Could you have the oven checked too?",
                      "I might get my hair cut while I'm there."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "passive_forms",
                    "title": "More passive forms: is being repaired, should be fixed",
                    "explanation": "La pasiva existe en todos los tiempos. Además de las formas que ya conoces («is repaired», «was repaired», «has been repaired», «will be repaired»):\n- Continua («being» + participio), algo que se está haciendo: «The boiler is being repaired right now.», «The kitchen was being repainted.» (cuando llegué, estaban pintando la cocina)\n- Con modales (modal + «be» + participio): «It should be fixed by Thursday.», «The oven must be checked.», «It can't be done today.»\n- Con «going to»: «The kitchen is going to be repainted next month.»\n- Infinitivo y gerundio: «The boiler needs to be replaced.», «I don't like being told what to do.»\n\nRecuerda: si importa quién lo hace, se añade «by»:\n- «It's being repaired by an engineer from Bath.»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Forma",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Present continuous",
                          "The boiler is being repaired."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Past continuous",
                          "The kitchen was being repainted when I arrived."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Modal",
                          "It should be fixed by Thursday."
                        ],
                        [
                          "going to",
                          "The kitchen is going to be repainted."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Infinitivo",
                          "The oven needs to be checked."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Gerundio",
                          "Nobody likes being woken up at six."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Sorry, no hot water. The boiler is being repaired.",
                      "The heating should be fixed by Thursday.",
                      "The kitchen is going to be repainted next month.",
                      "That oven needs to be checked. It's making a strange noise."
                    ]
                  }
                },
